droidasc-mcp

The caller grouping in src/droidasc_mcp/reference_groups.py is adapted from
aimardcr/asc-mcp, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Upstream: https://github.com/aimardcr/asc-mcp
Revision: 848c711f1d80a1c2577283f1fa5f475ff734aa40
Source: asc_mcp/analysis/asc_handler.py, AscHandler.findrefs_structured

Modifications retain droidasc-mcp's canonical caller/DEX identities and original
evidence fields, and group contiguous caller runs for ordered bounded pages.
Targets use first-appearance table indices and shared offset units live in group headers.
The Apache License, Version 2.0 is reproduced in LICENSE.

The AnalysisSession record and artifact inventory/capability flow in
src/droidasc_mcp/analysis_session.py are adapted from asc_mcp/sessions.py,
AnalysisSession and SessionRegistry.open, at the same upstream revision.
Handle formatting in AnalysisSession.handle and service.close_artifact is adapted
from asc_mcp/server.py, load_artifact and close_artifact.
The corresponding server tools, apk_get_summary, apk_get_manifest,
apk_list_entries, apk_get_resource_content and apk_get_signing_info retain
the upstream handle-oriented call pattern and matching argument names.
Adapted interfaces use existing bounded offset/byte continuations and the
128 KiB read cap, rather than upstream cursor and whole-document responses.

Modifications use supervised immutable snapshots and existing archive validation;
the registry lifecycle is integrated into DexSessions rather than a separate
registry. Snapshot and lazy DEX reservations, pinning, expiry, cancellation and
cleanup share the existing session owner. Content hashes bind archive reads and
lazy preparation to the loaded artifact, retaining original-path provenance.

The handle-oriented DEX wrappers in src/droidasc_mcp/focused_tools.py adapt
asc_mcp/server.py's apk_list_classes, class/source/structure tools, searches,
disassembly and call graph at the same revision. Query dispatch uses the existing
native session implementation rather than upstream worker/locator internals.
Modifications retain bounded offset pages, exact full identities, grouped cursors,
explicit overload errors and graph budgets. Partial/fuzzy member matching uses
apk_search_references; exact method/field tools retain precise selectors. Literal
string queries are passed unchanged to the native backend rather than regex-escaped.
Additional focused adapters retain every legacy DEX operation and broad type scope.
